-- title:
--   Residues of an embedding basis span the reduced Riemann–Roch space
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $R$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $N$ inside Laurent series) along $A$ onto $\widetilde F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N` (the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by the divisor expansions over $k$): that is, a valuation subring $R$.`integers` of $F$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R$.`residue` onto $\widetilde F$ with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction on $A$, a degree-preserving map $R$.`placeMap` on places, the scaling property that every nonzero $f\in F$ has a nonzero reduction after multiplication by some constant, and the clause that the divisor of the reduction of a unit is the pushforward of its divisor. Assume $R$ is good, i.e. $\mathrm{genusFF}(k,\widetilde F)=\mathrm{genusFF}(\overline{\mathbb Q},F)=:g$. Let $s:\mathrm{Fin}\,r\to F$ satisfy `IsEmbBasis N s`, i.e. $s$ is $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linearly independent and spans the Riemann–Roch space of $\mathrm{embDivisor}\,N=(2g+1)\cdot \mathrm{cuspInftyBar}\,N$; assume each $s_i$ lies in $R$.`integers` and that the residues $\overline{s_i}$ are $k$-linearly independent. Then the $k$-span of the $\overline{s_i}$ equals the Riemann–Roch space over $k$ of the pushforward divisor $R_*\bigl((2g+1)\cdot\mathrm{cuspInftyBar}\,N\bigr)$.
--
--   This is Deuring's comparison of a Riemann–Roch space with its reduction at a place of the constant field, specialised to the modular function field and to the divisor $(2g+1)\infty$ used to embed the curve; goodness of the reduction (equality of genera) is what makes the reduction of an embedding basis again a basis. It feeds the construction of reduced chart data for a constant reduction and, through that, the uniform description of dual graphs of coverings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_span_residue_eq_riemannRochSpace_of_isEmbBasis_of_isGood.lean

